WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.420
Each summer, part of the deep water in the Chesapeake Bay runs very low on oxygen.

2
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.660
Fish and crabs swim away from it.

3
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.580
Animals that cannot leave may get sick or die.

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.520
People call this low-oxygen water a dead zone.

5
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.800
How can too much fertilizer make part of the Bay run out of oxygen?

6
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.780
A nutrient is a substance living things need to grow.

7
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.660
Algae are tiny living things that grow in water.

8
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.260
They need nitrogen and phosphorus.

9
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.520
Farm fertilizer and manure contain these nutrients.

10
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.440
So does wastewater.

11
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.880
Rain washes nutrients from fields and lawns into rivers.

12
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:52.563
In the Bay, the extra nutrients feed the algae.

13
00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:54.563
They grow very fast.

14
00:00:55.403 --> 00:00:58.923
A thick, fast growth of algae is an algae bloom.

15
00:00:59.923 --> 00:01:02.943
The green water shades underwater grasses.

16
00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:06.183
Then the algae die and sink to the bottom.

17
00:01:07.416 --> 00:01:11.936
A decomposer is a living thing that breaks down dead matter.

18
00:01:12.816 --> 00:01:15.336
Bacteria decompose the dead algae.

19
00:01:16.096 --> 00:01:17.736
They use oxygen as they do.

20
00:01:18.716 --> 00:01:22.256
Dissolved oxygen is oxygen gas mixed into water.

21
00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:25.356
The deep water runs low on oxygen.

22
00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:32.400
In this lesson, a dead zone is water with less than two milligrams of oxygen per liter.

23
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.199
It is not empty.

24
00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:36.039
Bacteria live there.

25
00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:39.399
The water may hold little to no oxygen.

26
00:01:40.459 --> 00:01:42.639
Why the deep water, and why summer?

27
00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:46.499
Warm water can hold less dissolved oxygen.

28
00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:51.419
In summer, fresher river water floats on saltier Bay water.

29
00:01:51.419 --> 00:01:56.679
The layers mix poorly, so new oxygen reaches the deep water slowly.

30
00:01:57.599 --> 00:01:58.959
Here is the chain.

31
00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:02.179
Extra nutrients feed an algae bloom.

32
00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:04.719
The algae die and sink.

33
00:02:05.879 --> 00:02:09.779
Decomposers use the oxygen in deep water that does not mix.

34
00:02:10.859 --> 00:02:12.839
Fish and crabs often swim away.

35
00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.739
Animals that cannot leave may get sick or die.

36
00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:22.339
Eutrophication is extra nutrients feeding too much algae growth.

37
00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:24.519
It can lead to low oxygen.

38
00:02:25.309 --> 00:02:29.019
So fertilizer does not take oxygen from the Bay by itself.

39
00:02:29.739 --> 00:02:31.399
Its nutrients feed algae.

40
00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:34.099
Decomposers use the oxygen.
